{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176198": {
      "title": "Seasoned Assistant/Tenured Associate Professor in Finance",
      "description": "Department: Vanderbilt University: Owen Graduate School of Management Location: Nashville, TN  The Owen Graduate School of Management at Vanderbilt University is seeking applications for one position in the Finance group at the seasoned assistant/tenured associate level to begin August 2026. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in finance or closely related field from an AACSB accredited university. We seek candidates who have demonstrated the ability to conduct influential research, as measured by publications in top journals, as well as the ability to teach effectively. The Owen Graduate School of Management is engaged in graduate and undergraduate management education, with an enrollment of over 600 students in its MBA, Executive MBA, Master of Science in Finance, Master of Accountancy, Master of Marketing, and Master of Management in Health Care programs. In addition, Owen faculty members teach in the Vanderbilt University undergraduate business minor. Founded in 1873, Vanderbilt University is an internationally recognized research university with a student body of some 13,500 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students, and approximately 1,500 full-time faculty (excluding faculty employed by the Medical Center), of whom 55 have their primary appointment at Owen. Vanderbilt University is situated on a 330-acre campus located a mile and a half south of downtown Nashville. Home to more than 2.0 million people, the Nashville metropolitan statistical area has over a dozen colleges and universities. Nashville features many cultural and recreational amenities including a symphony orchestra, professional sports, an extensive park system, hiking and biking trails, exceptional restaurants, and live music offerings across a broad variety of genres. Major industries include healthcare, publishing, insurance and finance, higher education, and music. Nashville is frequently identified as one of the best U.S. cities for work, family, and quality of life by various national publications. We seek to attract research active, global-minded, and intellectually diverse faculty of the highest caliber, skilled in the scholarship of teaching, discovery, application, and integration of knowledge. Owen enrolls a student body from all parts of the U.S. and 47 countries. Both Owen and Vanderbilt University are fully committed to environments that are intellectually stimulating, dynamic, and that welcome well-being and community . Applicants should submit a letter of interest, a current vita, a statement of research and teaching interests, representative refereed publications, all working papers, and recent teaching evaluations. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Please direct questions about the search to Professor Berk Sensoy . All applications should be submitted to: https://apply.interfolio.com/176198"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188906": {
      "title": "Visiting Instructor of Mergers & Acquisitions",
      "description": "Department: Vanderbilt University: Owen Graduate School of Management Location: Nashville, TN  The Owen Graduate School of Management at Vanderbilt University invites applications for a visiting position to teach Mergers & Acquisitions in the spring semester of 2027. Preference will be given to applicants with a Ph.D. in finance from an AACSB accredited university and prior experience teaching Mergers & Acquisitions. The position will involve responsibility for teaching three sections of the course to our MBA and Master of Science in Finance students. The course will meet twice a week over a seven-week period. he Owen Graduate School of Management is engaged in graduate and undergraduate management education, with an enrollment of over 600 students in its MBA, Executive MBA, Master of Science in Finance, Master of Accountancy, Master of Marketing, and Master of Management in Health Care programs. In addition, Owen faculty members teach in the Vanderbilt University undergraduate business minor. Founded in 1873, Vanderbilt University is an internationally recognized research university with a student body of some 13,500 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students, and approximately 1,500 full-time faculty (excluding faculty employed by the Medical Center), of whom 55 have their primary appointment at Owen. Vanderbilt University is situated on a 330-acre campus located a mile and a half south of downtown Nashville. Home to more than 2.0 million people, the Nashville metropolitan statistical area has over a dozen colleges and universities. Nashville features many cultural and recreational amenities including a symphony orchestra, professional sports, an extensive park system, hiking and biking trails, exceptional restaurants, and live music offerings across a broad variety of genres. Major industries include healthcare, publishing, insurance and finance, higher education, and music. Nashville is frequently identified as one of the best U.S. cities for work, family, and quality of life by various national publications. We seek to attract research active, global-minded, and intellectually diverse faculty of the highest caliber, skilled in the scholarship of teaching, discovery, application, and integration of knowledge. Owen enrolls a student body from all parts of the U.S. and 47 countries. Both Owen and Vanderbilt University are fully committed to environments that are intellectually stimulating, dynamic, and that welcome well-being and community . Applications will be accepted immediately and on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Applicants should submit a letter of interest; a current curriculum vita; a statement of teaching experience, preferably with representative syllabi and student evaluations of courses taught; and three letters of reference. All initial interviews will be conducted virtually via Zoom. To ensure full consideration, please apply as soon as possible. If you have questions, please contact Professor Nicolas Bollen ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189202": {
      "title": "Advanced Assistant/Tenured Professors in Management",
      "description": "Department: Vanderbilt University: Owen Graduate School of Management Location: Nashville, TN  The Owen Graduate School of Management at Vanderbilt University is seeking applications for positions in the Management group at all ranks, including newly graduated PhD students, with a preference at the advanced assistant/tenured associate and professor level to begin August 2027. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in management, strategy, organizational behavior or closely related field from an AACSB accredited university. We seek candidates who have demonstrated the ability to conduct influential research, as measured by publications in top journals, as well as the ability to teach effectively. The Owen Graduate School of Management is engaged in graduate and undergraduate management education, with an enrollment of over 600 students in its MBA, Executive MBA, Master of Science in Finance, Master of Accountancy, Master of Marketing, and Master of Management in Health Care programs. In addition, Owen faculty members teach in the Vanderbilt University undergraduate business minor. Founded in 1873, Vanderbilt University is an internationally recognized research university with a student body of some 13,500 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students, and approximately 1,500 full-time faculty (excluding faculty employed by the Medical Center), of whom 55 have their primary appointment at Owen. Vanderbilt University is situated on a 330-acre campus located a mile and a half south of downtown Nashville. Vanderbilt University has also recently expanded or is in the process of expanding to New York, NY, West Palm Beach, FL, and San Francisco, CA. Home to more than 2.0 million people, the Nashville metropolitan statistical area has over a dozen colleges and universities. Nashville features many cultural and recreational amenities including a symphony orchestra, professional sports, an extensive park system, hiking and biking trails, exceptional restaurants, and live music offerings across a broad variety of genres. Major industries include healthcare, publishing, insurance and finance, higher education, and music. Nashville is frequently identified as one of the best U.S. cities for work, family, and quality of life by various national publications. We seek to attract research active, global-minded, and intellectually diverse faculty of the highest caliber, skilled in the scholarship of teaching, discovery, application, and integration of knowledge. Owen enrolls a student body from all parts of the U.S. and 47 countries. Both Owen and Vanderbilt University are fully committed to environments that are intellectually stimulating and dynamic. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in management, strategy, organizational behavior or closely related field from an AACSB accredited university. Applicants should submit a letter of interest, a current vita, a statement of research and teaching interests and recent teaching evaluations. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Please direct questions about the search to Tim Vogus (timothy.j.vogus@vanderbilt.edu). Review of applications will begin August 31 and continue until the positions are filled."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189718": {
      "title": "Visiting Instructor of Business Ethics",
      "description": "Department: Vanderbilt University: Owen Graduate School of Management Location: Nashville, TN  The Owen Graduate School of Management at Vanderbilt University invites applications for a visiting position to teach Ethics in Business in the spring semester of 2027. Preference will be given to applicants with a Ph.D. in management, organizational behavior, organization theory, business ethics, or related fields from an AACSB accredited university and prior experience teaching Ethics. The position will involve responsibility for teaching two sections of the course to our MBA students and one section to our EMBA students. The MBA course will meet twice a week over a seven-week period during the first half of the spring semester. The EMBA course will meet on Saturdays during the same period. The Owen Graduate School of Management is engaged in graduate and undergraduate management education, with an enrollment of over 600 students in its MBA, Executive MBA, Master of Science in Finance, Master of Accountancy, Master of Marketing, and Master of Management in Health Care programs. In addition, Owen faculty members teach in the Vanderbilt University undergraduate business minor. Founded in 1873, Vanderbilt University is an internationally recognized research university with a student body of some 13,500 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students, and approximately 1,500 full-time faculty (excluding faculty employed by the Medical Center), of whom 55 have their primary appointment at Owen. Vanderbilt University is situated on a 330-acre campus located a mile and a half south of downtown Nashville. Home to more than 2.0 million people, the Nashville metropolitan statistical area has over a dozen colleges and universities. Nashville features many cultural and recreational amenities including a symphony orchestra, professional sports, an extensive park system, hiking and biking trails, exceptional restaurants, and live music offerings across a broad variety of genres. Major industries include healthcare, publishing, insurance and finance, higher education, and music. Nashville is frequently identified as one of the best U.S. cities for work, family, and quality of life by various national publications. We seek to attract research active, global-minded, and intellectually diverse faculty of the highest caliber, skilled in the scholarship of teaching, discovery, application, and integration of knowledge. Owen enrolls a student body from all parts of the U.S. and 47 countries. Both Owen and Vanderbilt University are fully committed to environments that are intellectually stimulating, dynamic, and that welcome well-being and community . Preference will be given to applicants with a Ph.D. in management, organizational behavior, organization theory, business ethics, or related fields from an AACSB accredited university and prior experience teaching Ethics. Applications will be accepted immediately and on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Applicants should submit a letter of interest; a current curriculum vita; a statement of teaching experience, preferably with representative syllabi and student evaluations of courses taught. All initial interviews will be conducted virtually via Zoom. To ensure full consideration, please apply as soon as possible. If you have questions, please contact Professor Tim Vogus (timothy.j.vogus@vanderbilt.edu)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193526": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Positions in Accounting",
      "description": "Department: Vanderbilt University: Owen Graduate School of Management Location: Nashville, TN  The Owen Graduate School of Management at Vanderbilt University is seeking applications for two positions in the Accounting group. We will consider applications for all ranks, with a preference for the seasoned assistant/tenured associate level to begin in August 2027. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in accounting or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited university. We seek candidates who have demonstrated the ability to conduct influential research, as measured by publications in top journals, as well as the ability to teach effectively. The Owen Graduate School of Management is engaged in graduate and undergraduate management education, with an enrollment of over 600 students in its MBA, Executive MBA, Master of Science in Finance, Master of Accountancy, Master of Marketing, and Master of Management in Health Care programs. In addition, Owen faculty members teach in the Vanderbilt University undergraduate business minor. Founded in 1873, Vanderbilt University is an internationally recognized research university with a student body of some 13,500 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students, and approximately 1,500 full-time faculty (excluding faculty employed by the Medical Center), of whom 55 have their primary appointment at Owen. Vanderbilt University is situated on a 330-acre campus located a mile and a half south of downtown Nashville. Home to more than 2.0 million people, the Nashville metropolitan statistical area has over a dozen colleges and universities. Nashville features many cultural and recreational amenities including a symphony orchestra, professional sports, an extensive park system, hiking and biking trails, exceptional restaurants, and live music offerings across a broad variety of genres. Major industries include healthcare, publishing, insurance and finance, higher education, and music. Nashville is frequently identified as one of the best U.S. cities for work, family, and quality of life by various national publications. We seek to attract research active, global-minded, and intellectually diverse faculty of the highest caliber, skilled in the scholarship of teaching, discovery, application, and integration of knowledge. Owen enrolls a student body from all parts of the U.S. and 47 countries. Both Owen and Vanderbilt University are fully committed to environments that are intellectually stimulating, dynamic, and that welcome well-being and community . Applicants should submit a letter of interest, a current vita, a statement of research and teaching interests, representative refereed publications, all working papers, and recent teaching evaluations. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Please direct questions about the search to Daniel Cohen . Candidates must have a Ph.D. in accounting or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited university."
    },
